Outside this package's files: TraceSettingsControls.semantic.test.tsx,
flagged for the integrator.

Operator change: none; the dialog shows Remove ink specks at 2 for Line
Art, as the previous commit set. The test still proves that the control
reaches the engine without coupling to Ignore Less Than: at the default
the 3x2 detail (6 px) is kept (406 ink pixels), and raising the setting
to 7 removes it (400), where before it started at 12 and lowered to 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sve7yAMGfoSkUWytefCLp2
---
 src/ui/trace/TraceSettingsControls.semantic.test.tsx | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ui/trace/TraceSettingsControls.semantic.test.tsx b/src/ui/trace/TraceSettingsControls.semantic.test.tsx
index 6bf850baa..58124640c 100644
--- a/src/ui/trace/TraceSettingsControls.semantic.test.tsx
+++ b/src/ui/trace/TraceSettingsControls.semantic.test.tsx
@@ -132,12 +132,12 @@ describe('trace controls describe the options the engine actually receives', ()
     fill(image, 60, 40, 3, 2, [0, 0, 0]);
     await withControls('Line Art', async (controls) => {
       expect(controls.number('Ignore Less Than').value).toBe('2');
-      expect(controls.number('Remove ink specks').value).toBe('12');
-      expect(ink(preprocessForTrace(image, controls.options()))).toBe(400);
+      expect(controls.number('Remove ink specks').value).toBe('2');
+      expect(ink(preprocessForTrace(image, controls.options()))).toBe(406);
       await controls.change('Ignore Less Than', 3);
-      expect(ink(preprocessForTrace(image, controls.options()))).toBe(400);
-      await controls.change('Remove ink specks', 2);
       expect(ink(preprocessForTrace(image, controls.options()))).toBe(406);
+      await controls.change('Remove ink specks', 7);
+      expect(ink(preprocessForTrace(image, controls.options()))).toBe(400);
       expect(controls.options().ignoreLessThanPixels).toBe(3);
     });
   });
